From db2926f13f0f881c0eb35815e0ef82fc05d1c2f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:37:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] security: remove npm dependency-confusion packages pydantic
 and pandas

Both are Python library names resolved against the npm registry rather than
PyPI. Neither belongs in a Node manifest.

  pandas@0.0.3            unrelated 2012 Flickr photo-API client
  pydantic@0.0.1-security npm namespace-hold stub, empty package body

pyproject.toml already declares the real pydantic>=2.11.0; the Python side
was never affected.

Removed from dependencies in package.json and from every lockfile location
(root requirements, node_modules/pandas, node_modules/pydantic).

Static inspection found no install hook on either package - the only
hasInstallScript:true in the lockfile is this repo's own postinstall. All
ten files of node_modules/pandas were reviewed: no child_process, eval,
exec, process.env access, or network egress beyond a Flickr API call. No
evidence of credential exfiltration.

Outstanding, deliberately not in this commit:
  - node_modules/ is tracked (7,846 files) and no .gitignore exists
  - postinstall runs prettier --write . and eslint --fix ., mutating the
    working tree on every install

Refs: INCIDENT-2026-08-17-dependency-confusion.md
---
 package-lock.json | 13 -------------
 package.json      |  2 --
 2 files changed, 15 deletions(-)

